ation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163080942","title":"Obesity doesn’t equate to ill health: why the ‘disease’ label doesn’t always fit","authors":["Francesco Rubino"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7162988054","title":"Compliance modulation of a soft robotic atrioventricular model of heart failure with preserved ejection fraction","authors":["James Davies","Bibhu Sharma","Adrienne Ji","Gabriel Matus Vasquez","Chi Cong Nguyen","Emanuele Nicotra","Kefan Zhu","Phuoc Thien Phan","Jingjing Wan","Jelena Rnjak‐Kovacina","M. L. Stevens","Hoang‐Phuong Phan","Christopher Hayward","Nigel Hamilton Lovell","Thanh Nho"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-73791-w","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["HealthMon"],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163008564","title":"Population-specific heterogeneity in ontogeny of the broadly-conserved blood transcriptional program during the first week of life","authors":["Bhavjinder K. Dhillon","Travis M. Blimkie","Olubukola T. Idoko","Rebecca Ford","Asimenia Angelidou","Rym Ben-Othman","Sebastiano Montante","Nelly Amenyogbe","Tida Dibassey","Joann Diray‐Arce","Reza Falsafi","Abdulazeez Imam","Kerry McEnaney","Oludare A. Odumade","Al Ozonoff","William Pomat","Peter C. Richmond","Kinga K. Smolen","Oghenebrume Wariri","Ofer Levy","Anita H.J. van den Biggelaar","Beate Kampmann","Tobias Kollmann","Amy H. Y. Lee","Robert E. W. Hancock"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-73244-4","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163028655","title":"Self-supervised reservoir computing with spatial-temporal encoding for identifying critical transitions","authors":["N. Yang","J urgen Kurths","Rui Liu","Pei Chen"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-73182-1","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["HealthMon"],"_topics":["reservoir computing","critical transitions"],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"提出空间到时间自编码的储备池计算，用于识别临界转变。通过储备池结构进行空间到时间信息转换。","summary_en":"Proposes spatial-to-temporal auto reservoir computing for identifying critical transitions. Performs spatial-to-temporal information transformation via a reservoir structure.","insights":["创新点：提出空间到时间自编码的储备池计算","方法亮点：通过储备池结构进行信息转换","关键发现：识别临界转变"],"insights_en":["Novelty: Proposed spatial-to-temporal auto reservoir computing","Method highlight: Information transformation via a reservoir structure","Key finding: Identifying critical transitions"],"abstract":"Anticipating critical transitions and identifying bifurcation types in complex systems remains a major challenge due to high dimensionality and limited labeled data. In this study, we propose spatial-to-temporal auto reservoir computing, a self-supervised approach of reservoir computing designed to detect early warning signals of critical transitions and identify the corresponding bifurcation types, including transcritical, period-doubling, and Neimark-Sacker bifurcations. Grounded on Takens’ embedding theorem, it performs spatial-to-temporal information transformation via a reservoir structure, by encoding high-dimensional spatial data into the temporal dynamics of a single representative variable. This ultralow one-dimensional representation is obtained in a self-supervised and analytical manner, making it particularly suited for critical transition analyses in time-varying, high-dimensional systems. In addition, based on the Poincaré recurrence principle, the proposed method captures the structural information of the local phase space by constructing a spatial neighborhood network centered at each input state to enhance the robustness. The proposed method is validated on synthetic models and real-world datasets across multiple domains including paleoclimate, ecology and physiology, consistently achieving high accuracy and robustness under varying noise levels and parameter choices. Anticipating critical transitions is essential across diverse fields. Here, the authors propose a method, which enables early warning of critical transitions and identification of bifurcation types by converting high-dimensional spatial information into one-dimensional temporal dynamics."},{"id":"openalex:W7163064410","title":"The key role of an intramolecular non-classical hydrogen bond of vinylboron monomer for stereoselective polymerization","authors":["Hiroshi Suzuki","Tsuyoshi Nishikawa","Makoto Ouchi"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-73603-1","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163131497","title":"Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning for Pre-Trained Vision Models: A Survey and Benchmark","authors":["Yi Xin","Jianjiang Yang","Siqi Luo","Yuntao Du","Qi Qin","Haoxing Chen","Kangrui Cen","Yangfan He","Bin Fu","Yuewen Cao","Junjun He","Xiaokang Yang","Guangtao Zhai","Ming-Hsuan Yang","Xiaohong Liu"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"has_code":false,"type":"Survey","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"IJCV","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163138688","title":"Daily briefing: What it will take to stop the spiralling Ebola outbreak","authors":["Flora Graham"],"published":"2026-06-01","year":2026,"month":6,"has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7163154380","title":"Is